# Complete Trip Workspace and Itinerary Builder

This plan details the implementation of a fully interactive, local-state-driven Trip Workspace for GlobeTrotter. This is the core "travel planning canvas" of the application, focusing on visual itinerary building, dynamic timelines, and budget calculation.

## Proposed Changes

### State Management & Context
#### [MODIFY] `src/context/TripContext.tsx`
No structural changes are needed to the provider itself, but the consumer components will heavily utilize the existing `updateTrip` method. I will build utility functions inside the workspace to deep clone the `Trip` object, apply the necessary mutations (add/edit/delete/reorder stops and activities), and push the updated object to context.

### Workspace Core
#### [MODIFY] `src/pages/TripWorkspace.tsx`
- Implement the "Share Trip" modal containing the public link and copy button.
- Pass the `updateTrip` function down to the tabs so they can mutate the trip.
- Improve the Header to dynamically calculate the duration, number of cities, and display the trip cover image with proper fallbacks if Unsplash links break.

### The Itinerary Builder (CRITICAL)
#### [MODIFY] `src/components/workspace/ItineraryTab.tsx`
- **Route Visualizer:** Build the "Your Route" section showing stops connected visually (Rome ↓ Florence ↓ Venice).
- **Add Stop Modal:** Use Shadcn `Dialog` to create an "Add Stop" interface. Users can search `MOCK_CITIES`, select one, set arrival/departure dates, and append it to the trip.
- **Stop Controls:** Add "Edit", "Remove", and "Move Up/Down" buttons to reorder cities. Reordering will immediately swap the array indexes in the `trip.stops` array and call `updateTrip`.
- **Activity Management:** Add an "Add Activity" modal to each stop. Users can search `MOCK_ACTIVITIES`, pick a date/time, and add it. Implement "Edit Activity" and "Remove Activity" controls.
- **Day-Wise Itinerary:** Render the selected activities chronologically per day. Each day will clearly show Date → City → Activities → Time → Duration → Cost.

### Timeline & Calendar Views
#### [MODIFY] `src/components/workspace/CalendarTab.tsx`
- Implement a polished vertical Timeline view.
- Map all `trip.stops.activities` across the entire trip chronologically.
- Apply subtle visual treatments (e.g., specific icons/colors) based on the activity category (Sightseeing, Food, Culture, etc.).
- Ensure it feels like a readable, scannable timeline.

### Dynamic Budget Integration
#### [MODIFY] `src/components/workspace/BudgetTab.tsx`
- Tie the budget calculations directly to the activities in the itinerary.
- Dynamically calculate:
  - Total activity cost (sum of all activity costs)
  - Total estimated trip cost
  - Budget remaining
- When the user adds/removes activities in the Itinerary, the Budget tab will automatically reflect the changes via context.

### Overview & Public Share
#### [MODIFY] `src/components/workspace/OverviewTab.tsx`
- Add a visual route overview (e.g., Rome → Florence → Venice).
- Display summary statistics (Days, Cities, Activities, Total Cost).
#### [MODIFY] `src/pages/SharedTrip.tsx`
- Update the read-only public view to render the new day-wise timeline layout.
- Ensure the public page feels like a polished travel guide.

### Image Audit
- Implement a standard fallback for all `img` tags to ensure no broken browser placeholders appear if an Unsplash link fails.

